                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kreeck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-09T21:00:00-03:50"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1928—9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 11—12:22
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28. By the breaking of diplomatic relations Bolivia refuses to accept the Gondra
                    Treaty as set forth by Paraguay. The Paraguayan Government has the opinion that
                    Bolivia must accept the provisions of the Gondra Treaty to which both countries
                    are signatory parties. In the interest of peace and the purpose of the Kellogg
                    Pact, it is believed that the American Government should counsel Bolivia to
                    accept the provisions established in that treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kreeck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
